            "review_title": "Review at La Bodega",
            "review_text": "Abeomeomeo\n1 contribution\n2\nGood food, awesome place but AWFUL, BRUTAL OWNER\nJan 2022\nThe first time in my life I experienced such rude and brutal attitude from a restaurant owner (I heard that he’s also the chef)!!! \n\nThursday I booked a table for 8 (include elders and toddlers) for Sunday dinner. But when arrived, the receptionist said they don’t know anything, and there was no table left. When I showed them confirmed booking message from their restaurant, they took us to the table located right at the entrance, near the parking lot, which was kinda dark and separated from the dining area. I had no choice but to take it.\n\nThe restaurant owner then took me to my table, and when I start to complain a bit about the fact that they didn’t take note on my booking and I don’t really like this table, he CUT ME OFF and BRUTALLY TOLD ME TO GET OUT OF HIS RESTAURANT! \n\n“This is your table, IF YOU DON’T LIKE IT YOU CAN GO” – His finger point at my face with such rude attitude and angry look on his face, I felt like he was GOING TO PUNCH ME?\n\nWTH? It was a normal conversation and he throw this at my face??? My family (the elders and the toddlers) waited for 15 min then we had to go home right after we arrived like that.\n\nNo matter how awesome the place and the food was, I WILL NEVER EVER GOING BACK AND RECOMMEND ANYONE TO THIS RESTAURANT! \n\nIf you’re going to La Bodega, I hope you will look carefully at the restaurant owner and know that HE IS A VERY VERY RUDE, ARROGANT, BRUTAL PERSON and he DOESN’T DESERVE TO HAVE YOU AS A CUSTOMER!\n\nCheers.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 16, 2022",
