            "review_text": "Dion M\nHanoi, Vietnam200 contributions\n0\nA good concept, let down by poor service\nOct 2018 • Friends\nMet some friends out here for dinner, it’s a little tricky to find, so be prepared for that, look for the signs and you should be ok. It’s pretty child friendly out at this converted farm house, with swings, a climbing frame, a dodgy trampoline and lots of space. \nThe atmosphere and concept of this place is good, but it took over an hour for some simple pizzas to be made and tables that arrived after us were eating pizzas before we had received ours. After an hour and then asking how long our food would be, I was asked if I wanted spaghetti instead. Our order wasn’t filled correctly with mistakes and omissions from our initial order requests - when it did eventually come. Some of the food was tasty. This place could really benefit from a decent chef, (who can produce fast pizza turnaround and organize an efficient kitchen) and a big shake up of the FOH service standards, for example, nobody noticed or even seemed concerned that a table of 8 had been sitting for over an hour with no food. It was tough for the kids.\nSo we might try it again in 6 months or we may not. \nFresh, Wood fired pizzas are an amazing, simple food, but a business cannot survive on hit and miss service.\nRead more\nWritten October 21, 2018",
            "rating": 4.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
